  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1214 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nSfc high pressure is centered over the Ohio Valley this afternoon, \nproviding ample sunshine with comfortable humidity levels. \nIncreasing scattered mid-level cloud coverage tonight combined with \na subtle increase in the pressure gradient early Tuesday morning \nshould keep any patchy fog fairly sparse. By Wednesday,\ntemperatures will return to more seasonable with increasing \nhumidity levels as a warm front approaches from the south. \nRecent runs of the GFS/EC have trended more south with the \nboundary that would favor an elevated complex of storms \nremaining focused across AR/TN during the morning hours. NBM \nPoPs are now lower as a result, but still peak at a 20-30% \nchance Wednesday evening into Wednesday night in the wake of a \nweak cold front on Thursday. Low chances return over the \nKentucky Pennyrile Thursday afternoon, with a slight drop in \nhumidity levels being the only relief on Friday. \n\nMore significant levels of hot temperatures and humidity build \nnext weekend as a 594 dm southeast ridge causes height rises \naloft into early next week. By next Monday, 850 mb temps will be\npushing 20C which translates to highs in the mid 90s with heat \nindex values nearing the triple digits once again.",
